<title>USA: U.S. June PPI energy goods prices.</title>
<headline>U.S. June PPI energy goods prices.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Labor Department reported energy components of the producer price index as follows, with comparisons (1982=100 unless stated otherwise).</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				June    May   June97/96</p>
<p> Finished Energy Goods     0.7   -2.1     -1.3</p>
<p> -Gasoline		     0.4   -7.1     -5.9</p>
<p> -Heating Oil		 -5.8    2.2	1.3</p>
<p> -Residential Gas-Y	  1.8   -1.3	1.6</p>
<p>Y-Dec 1990=100.  </p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				June    May   June97/96</p>
<p> Intermed.Energy Goods     0.6   -1.9     -2.0</p>
<p> -Liq.Petroleum Gas-Z	1.6   -9.2	2.0</p>
<p> -Jet Fuel		     3.1   -6.2     -3.7</p>
<p> -Diesel Fuel		 -1.9   -2.7     -6.2</p>
<p> -Residual Fuel-Z	    3.4   13.4     -4.1</p>
<p>Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.  </p>
<p>   Percent Changes:    Seasonally Adj.  Unadjusted</p>
<p> -				June    May   June97/96</p>
<p> Crude Energy Materials   -2.9    3.4	1.8</p>
<p> -Coal-Z			 3.0   -6.4	2.8</p>
<p> -Natural Gas-Z		3.3    5.8     11.5</p>
<p> -Petroleum-Z		-14.1    7.3    -10.4</p>
<p>Note-Crude energy materials include crude petroleum. Z-Current data not seasonally adjusted.</p>
</text>
